<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĭpylus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σίπυλος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A mountain on the frontiers of Lydia and
			Phrygia</i>, <i>on which Niobe was changed into
			stone</i>, the modern <i>Manisa Dagh</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 2,
			20</span></i> (3, 13), 8; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6, 149</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Q. Fr.
				2, 11, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet. 184</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Agam. 374</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĭpylē-us</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Sipylus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genitrix Sipylea,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Niobe</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 5, 1, 33</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also called Sipyleïa cautes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Epit. 27</span></i>
			.—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĭpylen-sis</span></b> , e: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mater deorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ulp. Fragm. 22, 6</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A son of Niobe</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
				231</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
